### OptimalApi requests: run them top to bottom in Rider (click the green arrow next to each one).
### Start the API first: dotnet run --project src/OptimalApi.Api

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Create a product (saves its id and version for the requests below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "price": 89.99
}

> {%
    client.global.set("productId", response.body.data.id);
    client.global.set("version", response.body.data.version);
%}

### 2. Get it by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 3. List products (page 1, 20 per page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=1&pageSize=20

### 4. Update it, sending the version from the last read
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard (RGB)",
  "price": 99.99,
  "version": {{version}}
}

> {%
    client.global.set("staleVersion", client.global.get("version"));
    client.global.set("version", response.body.data.version);
%}

### 5. Update with the old (stale) version -> 409 Conflict
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someone else's edit",
  "price": 1.00,
  "version": {{staleVersion}}
}

### 6. Invalid body -> 400 with field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "price": -5
}

### 7. Page size too big -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?pageSize=1000

### 8. Unknown id -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 9. Delete it -> 200
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 10. Delete again -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 11. Health: every check with details (Development only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 12. Health: readiness (what Docker/Kubernetes use)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### The dashboard is a web page: open {{baseUrl}}/health-ui in your browser.
